WEBVTT

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:04.969
Last time on
Star Trek: Deep Space Nine...

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.529
If you could do any
science project you wanted to

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.303
anything at all...

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:10.969
Visit the Gamma Quadrant?

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.919
We've never heard
of the Jem'Hadar.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.550
Then you've been fortunate.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:30.495
Negotiations with the Dominion
can be a dangerous thing.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.990
The Dominion will
no longer stand by

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:38.766
and allow ships from your side
to violate our territory.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.432
Starfleet's orders are simple.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.532
Traffic through the wormhole
will be suspended

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.008
until the Odyssey
can investigate

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.409
the Jem'Hadar's threat.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.935
What about Benjamin
and the others?

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.607
Don't worry, Lieutenant.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.014
Commander Sisko's return
is a top priority.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.574
If you're going to try
to rescue them

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:53.745
then we're coming with you.

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:05.356
Here they come.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.302
Major, one
of the Jem'Hadar ships

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.808
is making a direct run
at the Odyssey.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.679
The Jem'Hadar wanted us
to escape, didn't they?

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.347
You have no idea
what's begun here.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.624
She'll be back.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:34.889
The question is
who she'll bring with her.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.829
If the Dominion
comes through the wormhole

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:40.332
the first battle
will be fought here

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.665
and I intend
to be ready for them.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:46.536
And now, the continuation.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.684
We're in trouble, people.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.950
We've run seven simulations
and they all come out the same.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.854
The Jem'Hadar
overwhelm our defenses

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.950
and board the station
within two hours.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.756
Two hours doesn't even
give us time

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.456
to get reinforcements
from Bajor.

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.624
There must be something
we overlooked.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.133
Major, I'm the last one
to say it's hopeless

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.636
but given DS9's
structural limitations

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.137
our available power supply

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.732
and the difficulty of defending
a stationary target

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.537
against a heavily
armed mobile force

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.441
I'd say two hours is optimistic.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.809
Well, regardless of the time

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.404
the casualties
would be appalling.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:31.076
All right, let's say we let
them board the station.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.982
That still doesn't mean
we have to surrender.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.452
What are you suggesting?

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.785
We can, uh...

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:40.190
we can hide in the conduits,
set up booby traps

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.456
prepare ambushes...
try and hold out

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.520
until we can get
reinforcements.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.997
We can try,
but I don't think

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.659
there'd be
much of a station left

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.997
by the time they got here.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.332
That leaves us
with two options...

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:54.602
abandon the station
and make a stand on Bajor.

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:59.169
Or... collapse the entrance
to the wormhole.

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:00.645
No, I want a third alternative.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.170
I cannot believe
that we can't...

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:09.486
Some kind of large subspace
surge has just activated

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.580
our security sensors.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:11.590
Where is it?

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.683
Bearing 148 mark 215.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.421
Distance 300 meters.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:16.951
300 meters?

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.692
That's almost inside
our shield perimeter.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.565
From the intensity
in the harmonic signature

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:24.263
it could be a cloaked ship

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:27.398
but I've never seen an energy
dispersal pattern like this.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.169
It's too close for comfort,
whatever it is.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.176
Red Alert.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.177
Raise shields.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.576
Energize phaser banks.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.704
Stand by to lock
photon torpedoes.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.976
The energy
signature's fluctuating.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.107
It's de-cloaking.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.282
It's definitely
a Federation starship

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:47.259
but I've never seen
that design before.

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.727
A Federation ship
with a cloaking device?

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:50.990
It's hailing us.

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.395
On screen.

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:54.325
Hello, Major.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.857
Sorry to startle you,
but I wanted

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.597
to test the Defiant's
cloaking device.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.400
The Defiant?

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:02.567
I've brought back a little
surprise for the Dominion.

00:06:08.498 --> 00:06:11.661
Officially, it's classified
as an escort vessel.

00:06:11.702 --> 00:06:15.263
Unofficially,
the Defiant's a warship...

00:06:15.305 --> 00:06:17.830
nothing more, nothing less.

00:06:17.874 --> 00:06:20.035
I thought Starfleet
didn't believe in warships.

00:06:20.077 --> 00:06:23.240
Desperate times breed
desperate measures, Major.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:27.080
Five years ago, Starfleet
began exploring the possibility

00:06:27.117 --> 00:06:29.483
of building
a new class of starship.

00:06:29.519 --> 00:06:32.420
This ship would have
no families, no science labs

00:06:32.456 --> 00:06:34.447
no luxuries of any kind.

00:06:34.491 --> 00:06:36.652
It was designed
for one purpose only...

00:06:36.693 --> 00:06:38.786
to fight and defeat the Borg.

00:06:38.829 --> 00:06:40.558
The Defiant was a prototype.

00:06:40.597 --> 00:06:42.656
The first ship
in what would have been

00:06:42.699 --> 00:06:44.098
a new Federation battle fleet.

00:06:44.134 --> 00:06:45.533
So what happened?

00:06:45.569 --> 00:06:47.764
The Borg threat
became less urgent.

00:06:47.804 --> 00:06:49.931
Also, some design flaws
cropped up

00:06:49.973 --> 00:06:52.373
during the ship's
shakedown cruise

00:06:52.409 --> 00:06:54.843
so Starfleet decided
to abandon the project.

00:06:54.878 --> 00:06:56.368
What sort of design flaws?

00:06:56.413 --> 00:06:59.712
You'll have complete access
to the ship evaluation reports

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.843
but, to put it simply,
it's overgunned

00:07:01.885 --> 00:07:03.910
and overpowered
for a ship its size.

00:07:03.954 --> 00:07:06.889
During battle drills,
it nearly tore itself apart

00:07:06.923 --> 00:07:08.914
when the engines were tested
at full capacity.

00:07:08.992 --> 00:07:11.756
And this is the ship
that Starfleet sends us

00:07:11.795 --> 00:07:13.456
to fight off an attack
by the Dominion?

00:07:13.497 --> 00:07:16.398
We're not going to fight
the Dominion, Major

00:07:16.433 --> 00:07:18.094
at least, not yet anyway.

00:07:18.135 --> 00:07:22.094
Our mission is to take the
Defiant into the Gamma Quadrant

00:07:22.139 --> 00:07:25.905
and try to find the leaders
of the Dominion, the Founders.

00:07:25.942 --> 00:07:27.569
We have to convince them
that the Federation

00:07:27.611 --> 00:07:28.942
does not represent
a threat to them.

00:07:28.979 --> 00:07:31.846
What if they don't believe us?

00:07:31.882 --> 00:07:34.373
That's why I asked
for the Defiant.

00:07:34.418 --> 00:07:37.080
She may have flaws,
but she has teeth

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.384
and I want the Dominion to know

00:07:39.423 --> 00:07:43.223
that we can and will defend
ourselves, if necessary.

00:07:45.295 --> 00:07:46.956
I've posted
two security officers

00:07:46.997 --> 00:07:49.761
at the Defiant's
docking port, sir.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.324
No one will get near
the cloaking device

00:07:51.368 --> 00:07:52.460
without us knowing about it.

00:07:52.502 --> 00:07:53.901
I wasn't informed

00:07:53.937 --> 00:07:56.633
about any special
security arrangements.

00:07:56.673 --> 00:07:59.369
The security arrangements
were by my request

00:07:59.409 --> 00:08:01.843
to protect the cloaking device.

00:08:01.878 --> 00:08:03.505
A few introductions
are in order.

00:08:03.547 --> 00:08:06.072
This is Subcommander T'Rul,
from the Romulan Empire.

00:08:06.116 --> 00:08:08.175
She's here to operate
the cloaking device

00:08:08.218 --> 00:08:09.378
which her government

00:08:09.419 --> 00:08:11.580
so kindly loaned us
for this mission.

00:08:11.621 --> 00:08:14.590
Romulan interests will be
served through cooperation

00:08:14.624 --> 00:08:17.149
and my role is to keep
unauthorized personnel

00:08:17.194 --> 00:08:18.923
away from the cloaking device.

00:08:18.962 --> 00:08:20.452
May I present my officers.

00:08:20.497 --> 00:08:21.589
This is Major Ki...

00:08:21.631 --> 00:08:24.031
Thank you,
but I know their names

00:08:24.067 --> 00:08:26.433
and I'm not here
to make friends.

00:08:29.639 --> 00:08:31.038
Charming.

00:08:31.074 --> 00:08:33.838
Well, I am here to make friends.

00:08:33.877 --> 00:08:37.677
I'm Lieutenant Commander
Michael Eddington

00:08:37.714 --> 00:08:39.443
Starfleet Security.

00:08:39.483 --> 00:08:41.883
Major Kira Nerys.

00:08:45.555 --> 00:08:49.286
Odo, Head of Station Security.

00:08:49.326 --> 00:08:52.659
May I ask what your function
is here, Commander?

00:08:52.696 --> 00:08:54.721
There will be
a complete mission briefing

00:08:54.764 --> 00:08:56.425
at 1800 hours, but be prepared

00:08:56.466 --> 00:08:59.128
to depart the station
at 0700 tomorrow morning.

00:08:59.169 --> 00:09:00.329
Dismissed.

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:08.302
You needn't brace yourself

00:09:08.345 --> 00:09:10.711
to give me
unpleasant news, Commander.

00:09:10.747 --> 00:09:12.374
I'll save you the trouble.

00:09:12.415 --> 00:09:15.350
I've been relieved
as Chief of Security.

00:09:19.289 --> 00:09:20.256
Odo, wait!

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:21.257
You've not been relieved.

00:09:21.291 --> 00:09:22.588
You're still in charge

00:09:22.626 --> 00:09:24.753
of all non-Starfleet security
matters aboard this station.

00:09:24.794 --> 00:09:26.887
And what about matters
that are Starfleet?

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:28.591
In those areas,
you coordinate your efforts

00:09:28.632 --> 00:09:29.621
with Commander Eddington.

00:09:29.666 --> 00:09:31.566
"Coordinate" is
another way of saying

00:09:31.601 --> 00:09:32.625
I'll report to him.

00:09:34.871 --> 00:09:35.929
I'm sorry, Odo.

00:09:36.039 --> 00:09:37.336
This wasn't my idea.

00:09:37.374 --> 00:09:38.671
I'm sure it wasn't.

00:09:38.708 --> 00:09:40.266
You were just
following orders.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:42.403
An order I strongly
disagreed with.

00:09:42.445 --> 00:09:45.073
I did everything
I could to fight this.

00:09:45.115 --> 00:09:46.275
I even took it

00:09:46.316 --> 00:09:48.477
to the Chief of Starfleet
Security herself

00:09:48.518 --> 00:09:50.247
but the decision was final.

00:09:50.287 --> 00:09:52.312
May I ask why?

00:09:52.355 --> 00:09:53.379
There were some concerns

00:09:53.423 --> 00:09:56.017
about several recent
security breaches.

00:09:57.227 --> 00:09:59.593
If I was given
the authority I asked for

00:09:59.629 --> 00:10:02.393
instead of being tied
to Starfleet regulations

00:10:02.432 --> 00:10:05.265
there wouldn't have been
any security breaches.

00:10:05.302 --> 00:10:07.293
Odo, your resistance to
following Starfleet regulations

00:10:07.337 --> 00:10:08.964
is part of the problem.

00:10:09.005 --> 00:10:12.463
Well, I think there might be a
simpler explanation, Commander.

00:10:12.509 --> 00:10:14.409
I think Starfleet
decided to bring in

00:10:14.444 --> 00:10:15.934
someone they could trust...

00:10:15.979 --> 00:10:19.972
someone besides
"the shape-shifter."

00:10:20.016 --> 00:10:23.247
This is not a racial issue, Odo.

00:10:23.286 --> 00:10:25.550
I understand
how you must feel, and I...

00:10:25.589 --> 00:10:26.886
Commander.

00:10:26.923 --> 00:10:29.892
I don't require
your understanding.

00:10:29.926 --> 00:10:33.919
My resignation will be logged
within the hour.

00:10:46.042 --> 00:10:47.009
Hey, hey, hey...

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:48.668
I thought you were unpacking.

00:10:48.712 --> 00:10:49.804
I am.
I mean, I was.

00:10:49.846 --> 00:10:52.542
But I just kept looking
at the replicator and...

00:10:52.582 --> 00:10:54.948
And you just had to have
some I'danian spice pudding.

00:10:54.985 --> 00:10:56.009
You know, I still can't believe

00:10:56.086 --> 00:10:57.576
I couldn't get a decent bowl
back on Earth.

00:10:57.621 --> 00:10:59.680
That didn't stop you
from ordering it

00:10:59.723 --> 00:11:01.315
at every replicator you saw.

00:11:01.358 --> 00:11:02.950
So...

00:11:02.993 --> 00:11:04.585
is it good to be home?

00:11:04.628 --> 00:11:05.754
Yeah.

00:11:05.795 --> 00:11:07.820
I can't wait to sleep
in my own bed again.

00:11:08.865 --> 00:11:10.457
Whew.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:13.128
I wonder when that happened.

00:11:13.169 --> 00:11:14.636
What?

00:11:14.671 --> 00:11:19.165
When did I start thinking
of this Cardassian monstrosity

00:11:19.209 --> 00:11:21.302
as home?

00:11:21.344 --> 00:11:23.505
I think it happened...

00:11:23.546 --> 00:11:25.070
last Thursday.

00:11:25.115 --> 00:11:28.175
Around 1700 hours...

00:11:28.218 --> 00:11:31.312
when you took all of this stuff
out of storage back on Earth.

00:11:31.354 --> 00:11:34.551
I... Careful, that's
a 2,000-year-old Yoruba mask

00:11:34.591 --> 00:11:37.560
and that "stuff" is one
of the finest collections

00:11:37.594 --> 00:11:38.822
of ancient African art...

00:11:38.862 --> 00:11:40.489
You'll ever see.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:41.622
I know.

00:11:41.665 --> 00:11:43.997
And I also know
how much it means to you.

00:11:44.067 --> 00:11:45.967
But, to me, this will always be

00:11:46.002 --> 00:11:48.436
the stuff in your library...
at home.

00:11:48.471 --> 00:11:52.271
When you took it out of storage
so you could bring it here

00:11:52.309 --> 00:11:55.005
it meant that Earth
wasn't home anymore.

00:11:55.045 --> 00:11:56.979
This was.

00:12:01.718 --> 00:12:02.810
So...

00:12:04.154 --> 00:12:05.678
what do you think?

00:12:06.856 --> 00:12:08.153
Perfect.

00:12:19.669 --> 00:12:20.693
Odo.

00:12:20.737 --> 00:12:21.897
There you are.

00:12:21.938 --> 00:12:24.668
I just finished talking
to the provisional government

00:12:24.708 --> 00:12:27.233
and they want you to go with us
to the Gamma Quadrant tomorrow

00:12:27.277 --> 00:12:29.177
to act as an official
Bajoran representative.

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.147
I'm no diplomat.

00:12:31.181 --> 00:12:32.148
I know.

00:12:32.182 --> 00:12:34.116
That's why they want you to go.

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:35.378
If we do locate the Founders

00:12:35.418 --> 00:12:37.147
we're going to need
more than diplomacy.

00:12:37.187 --> 00:12:38.711
We're going to need
to size them up

00:12:38.755 --> 00:12:40.188
see what kind
of threat they pose

00:12:40.223 --> 00:12:41.212
to Bajor, analyze...

00:12:41.257 --> 00:12:44.090
You're the military
expert, Major, not me.

00:12:44.127 --> 00:12:47.392
And I doubt

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:50.160
that the provisional
government contacted you

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.863
and asked for my presence
on this mission.

00:12:53.903 --> 00:12:55.272
If I'm not mistaken

00:12:55.405 --> 00:12:58.806
this is a misguided attempt
to make me feel better.

00:12:58.842 --> 00:13:01.208
Maybe it is.

00:13:02.412 --> 00:13:05.279
Maybe I'm your friend.

00:13:05.315 --> 00:13:07.044
And maybe I want you to see

00:13:07.083 --> 00:13:09.176
that you are still
needed here...

00:13:09.219 --> 00:13:14.316
no matter what some idiot
Starfleet admiral might think.

00:13:25.835 --> 00:13:29.236
The Defiant leaves at 700 hours.

00:13:44.287 --> 00:13:48.417
I'm a little confused,
Commander.

00:13:48.458 --> 00:13:52.121
You want me to go with you
to the Gamma Quadrant

00:13:52.162 --> 00:13:55.359
to help you locate
the Founders.

00:13:55.398 --> 00:13:58.993
See? It's not
so confusing after all.

00:13:59.069 --> 00:14:00.832
You're joking with me,
aren't you?

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.360
Having a little fun with Quark.

00:14:02.405 --> 00:14:03.565
I'm quite serious.

00:14:03.606 --> 00:14:04.664
You can't be.

00:14:04.708 --> 00:14:06.039
I'm not a diplomat

00:14:06.076 --> 00:14:08.704
or an explorer
or a tactical officer

00:14:08.745 --> 00:14:11.475
or whatever else you
might need on this trip.

00:14:11.514 --> 00:14:14.813
Now, if you need a caterer,
I'd be happy to loan you

00:14:14.851 --> 00:14:17.081
a new replicator
that I just got...

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.452
Eight months ago,
you helped the Nagus

00:14:19.489 --> 00:14:22.617
establish a trade agreement
with the Karemma, uh...

00:14:22.659 --> 00:14:25.253
tulaberry wine, I believe.

00:14:25.295 --> 00:14:27.695
The Karemma are
part of the Dominion.

00:14:27.731 --> 00:14:29.858
A minor part...
a very minor part.

00:14:29.899 --> 00:14:31.457
They might still
be able to help us

00:14:31.501 --> 00:14:32.866
make contact with the Founders.

00:14:32.902 --> 00:14:35.302
Since you're experienced
in dealing with the Karemma,

00:14:35.338 --> 00:14:37.499
it seems to me that you're
the logical person...

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.565
Actually, my brother Rom
did most of the talking.

00:14:39.609 --> 00:14:41.839
I think he'd be better suited
for this mission.

00:14:41.878 --> 00:14:43.607
Not Rom... you.

00:14:43.646 --> 00:14:44.635
But why?

00:14:44.681 --> 00:14:47.411
Rom only has a son
to think about.

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:48.974
I have a business.

00:14:49.986 --> 00:14:51.010
You.

00:14:53.123 --> 00:14:57.958
I'm sorry, Commander,
but I must refuse.

00:14:57.994 --> 00:15:00.588
My last experience
with the Jem'Hadar

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:02.154
was not a pleasant one

00:15:02.198 --> 00:15:04.928
and I have no intention
of repeating it.

00:15:05.034 --> 00:15:09.903
Now, there's no way you can
legally force me to do this.

00:15:14.911 --> 00:15:17.038
The scepter of the Grand Nagus.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:19.947
I had a chance to discuss
this mission with him

00:15:20.049 --> 00:15:21.710
on my way back from Earth.

00:15:21.751 --> 00:15:23.048
He seemed to agree with me.

00:15:23.086 --> 00:15:24.212
Unless peaceful contact

00:15:24.254 --> 00:15:26.222
can be established
with the Founders

00:15:26.256 --> 00:15:28.554
business opportunities
in the Gamma Quadrant

00:15:28.591 --> 00:15:29.922
might suddenly dry up.

00:15:29.959 --> 00:15:34.658
He also agreed with me that you
are the perfect man to help me.

00:15:34.697 --> 00:15:36.722
I don't believe it.

00:15:36.766 --> 00:15:38.131
Which is why he sent this along.

00:15:38.168 --> 00:15:39.533
He thought it might convince you

00:15:39.569 --> 00:15:44.404
of the high value he holds
for the success of this mission.

00:15:45.542 --> 00:15:46.907
Now...

00:15:46.943 --> 00:15:48.808
are you going to defy

00:15:48.845 --> 00:15:52.281
the wishes of the Grand Nagus
himself?

00:15:52.315 --> 00:15:53.976
No, no... of course not.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:57.110
I'm happy to serve the Nagus
any way I can.

00:15:57.153 --> 00:15:58.120
Thanks, Quark.

00:15:58.154 --> 00:15:59.678
I knew I could count on you.

00:15:59.722 --> 00:16:01.189
Yeah.

00:16:02.525 --> 00:16:04.550
Quark?

00:16:04.594 --> 00:16:06.494
Aren't you forgetting something?

00:16:08.298 --> 00:16:09.788
Oh.

00:16:38.294 --> 00:16:39.955
I just thought
you'd like to know.

00:16:40.029 --> 00:16:42.054
The Defiant will be
ready at 0700 hours.

00:16:42.098 --> 00:16:43.531
Did it pass
the Chief's inspection?

00:16:43.566 --> 00:16:44.590
Does anything?

00:16:44.634 --> 00:16:46.534
His maintenance list
is as long as this table.

00:16:46.569 --> 00:16:48.628
But he did say it will
take us where we're going.

00:16:48.671 --> 00:16:51.731
And back, I hope.

00:16:51.774 --> 00:16:53.639
Well, he said
that was up to you.

00:16:53.676 --> 00:16:56.076
I'd never have volunteered
for this mission

00:16:56.112 --> 00:16:58.979
if I didn't think we had
a chance of coming back.

00:16:59.015 --> 00:17:01.245
How many times
did Curzon tell you

00:17:01.284 --> 00:17:03.184
never volunteer for anything?

00:17:03.219 --> 00:17:06.711
As I recall, Curzon broke
that rule a few times himself.

00:17:06.756 --> 00:17:08.781
And regretted it every time.

00:17:08.825 --> 00:17:10.417
This is different.

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.451
I'd be regretting it even more

00:17:12.495 --> 00:17:15.259
if we just waited around
for an invasion.

00:17:21.070 --> 00:17:23.732
If I know Starfleet,
they must have run

00:17:23.773 --> 00:17:28.039
at least 200 probability studies
on this mission of ours.

00:17:28.077 --> 00:17:30.944
So what are the odds
of us succeeding?

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.914
Slim.

00:17:35.118 --> 00:17:37.245
But better odds
than fighting off

00:17:37.287 --> 00:17:39.653
a Jem'Hadar assault
on this station.

00:17:39.689 --> 00:17:42.487
And if the station falls,
then Bajor falls

00:17:42.525 --> 00:17:44.652
and I will not let that happen.

00:17:47.096 --> 00:17:50.395
You know, after Jennifer died

00:17:50.433 --> 00:17:53.630
I never thought I would
see you this passionate

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.331
about something again.

00:17:55.371 --> 00:17:58.829
Two months ago, I would
have agreed with you.

00:17:58.875 --> 00:18:00.900
Then I went back to Earth

00:18:00.944 --> 00:18:04.107
and I spent all
those weeks debriefing

00:18:04.147 --> 00:18:06.411
at Starfleet Headquarters.

00:18:06.449 --> 00:18:07.507
And I...

00:18:09.385 --> 00:18:13.048
I used to get a thrill
just walking into that building.

00:18:13.089 --> 00:18:15.182
I'd look around at the admirals

00:18:15.224 --> 00:18:18.057
and think, "One day,
that's going to be me.

00:18:18.094 --> 00:18:19.459
"One day, I'm the one

00:18:19.495 --> 00:18:22.521
that's going to be making
the big decisions."

00:18:24.233 --> 00:18:26.599
Curzon always thought
that was very funny.

00:18:26.636 --> 00:18:27.603
Did he?

00:18:27.637 --> 00:18:28.934
What I mean is

00:18:29.038 --> 00:18:32.940
he could never see a set of
admiral stars on your collar.

00:18:33.009 --> 00:18:35.876
He thought that just
making the decisions

00:18:35.912 --> 00:18:37.607
would never satisfy you.

00:18:37.647 --> 00:18:39.581
You had to implement them...

00:18:39.616 --> 00:18:43.780
see the results,
face the consequences.

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:47.153
Curzon always thought
you were the kind of man

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:49.784
who had to be
in the thick of things...

00:18:49.826 --> 00:18:52.795
not behind some desk
at Headquarters.

00:18:56.099 --> 00:19:00.536
He was a smart old man,
wasn't he?

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:03.038
He'd like to think so.

00:19:07.377 --> 00:19:10.210
You'd better get
a good night's sleep.

00:19:10.246 --> 00:19:13.238
I was just about to say
the same thing to you.

00:19:13.282 --> 00:19:15.773
I'll see you
in the morning, Benjamin.

00:19:27.497 --> 00:19:30.057
The medical database
is practically nonexistent.

00:19:30.099 --> 00:19:31.691
I've downloaded
as many of my files

00:19:31.734 --> 00:19:32.928
from the station as I can

00:19:32.969 --> 00:19:34.630
but this ship
simply wasn't designed

00:19:34.671 --> 00:19:35.933
to handle many casualties.

00:19:35.972 --> 00:19:37.530
Do the best you can,
and let's hope we don't

00:19:37.573 --> 00:19:39.438
have to put your new
database to a test.

00:19:39.475 --> 00:19:40.601
Yes, sir.

00:19:40.643 --> 00:19:42.076
Quark's settling
into his quarters

00:19:42.111 --> 00:19:46.047
and asked me to relay to you
his profound disappointment

00:19:46.082 --> 00:19:48.516
in the accommodations,
and to inform you

00:19:48.551 --> 00:19:49.950
that he could
get you in touch

00:19:50.019 --> 00:19:52.112
with several reputable
interior decorators

00:19:52.155 --> 00:19:53.679
for a modest fee.

00:19:53.723 --> 00:19:55.918
I'll take his offer
under advisement.

00:19:55.958 --> 00:19:57.721
Stand by to get underway.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.955
Tactical and communications
are ready, sir.

00:20:00.063 --> 00:20:02.224
Navigation and operations,
ready.

00:20:02.265 --> 00:20:03.833
Weapons ready.

00:20:03.966 --> 00:20:05.331
Impulse engines on-line.

00:20:05.367 --> 00:20:06.732
Warp power available
at your command.

00:20:06.769 --> 00:20:08.396
Very well.

00:20:08.437 --> 00:20:11.201
Seal the airlock,
release docking clamps, aft...

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:12.969
Just a moment, sir.

00:20:13.042 --> 00:20:15.977
There's someone in the airlock.

00:20:16.011 --> 00:20:17.273
It's Odo.

00:20:19.548 --> 00:20:20.606
Sisko to Odo.

00:20:20.649 --> 00:20:22.583
Is there a problem, Constable?

00:20:22.618 --> 00:20:26.076
No, Commander. I would like
permission to come aboard.

00:20:26.121 --> 00:20:31.218
I'm here at the request
of the Bajoran government.

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:32.591
Permission granted.

00:20:32.628 --> 00:20:34.619
Thank you, sir.

00:20:34.663 --> 00:20:37.427
Dax, we'll have to arrange
some quarters for the Constable.

00:20:37.466 --> 00:20:38.660
I'll do it, sir.

00:20:38.701 --> 00:20:41.636
I need to go down to what is
laughingly called the Sick Bay.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:42.728
Thank you, Doctor.

00:20:42.771 --> 00:20:43.999
Odo's aboard, sir.

00:20:44.073 --> 00:20:45.267
The airlock's clear.

00:20:45.307 --> 00:20:46.706
Release docking clamps.

00:20:46.742 --> 00:20:48.505
Aft thrusters at one quarter.

00:20:48.544 --> 00:20:50.876
Port and starboard
at station keeping.

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:09.357
We've cleared the station.

00:21:09.398 --> 00:21:11.423
Lay in a course
to the wormhole.

00:21:11.467 --> 00:21:13.298
I want to cloak as soon as
we reach the Gamma Quadrant.

00:21:13.335 --> 00:21:14.495
Understood.

00:21:15.738 --> 00:21:17.603
Course laid in, sir.

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:19.665
Engage.

00:21:43.799 --> 00:21:48.259
The cloaking device is operating
within normal parameters.

00:21:48.304 --> 00:21:50.898
Set course
for the Karemma system.

00:21:50.940 --> 00:21:51.998
Warp 7.

00:21:52.041 --> 00:21:53.008
Aye, sir.

00:21:53.042 --> 00:21:54.373
Engage.

00:21:57.479 --> 00:21:58.537
Odo!

00:22:02.184 --> 00:22:04.778
Is this the best you can do?

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:06.378
I'm afraid so.

00:22:06.422 --> 00:22:08.890
Most of the crew quarters
don't have life supports yet.

00:22:08.924 --> 00:22:11.188
Besides, I think
we'd all feel a bit better

00:22:11.226 --> 00:22:13.251
with someone here
to watch over Quark.

00:22:13.295 --> 00:22:16.787
I take that
as a personal insult, Doctor.

00:22:16.832 --> 00:22:18.493
You should.

00:22:18.534 --> 00:22:21.628
Now, I think
I'll let you two bunkmates

00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:23.399
get more comfortable.

00:22:25.474 --> 00:22:26.702
Am I glad to see you.

00:22:26.742 --> 00:22:29.802
I have been stuck
down here in this miserable hole

00:22:29.845 --> 00:22:31.506
ever since I came on board.

00:22:31.547 --> 00:22:32.571
Bunk beds!

00:22:32.614 --> 00:22:33.774
No view.

00:22:33.816 --> 00:22:35.977
And I can't tell
you what came out

00:22:36.051 --> 00:22:39.111
of that replicator when
I asked for synthehol.

00:22:41.457 --> 00:22:42.719
So...

00:22:42.758 --> 00:22:45.750
what's your role
in this little adventure?

00:22:45.794 --> 00:22:48.319
Providing security, no doubt.

00:22:48.364 --> 00:22:50.457
Well, of course you are.

00:22:50.499 --> 00:22:53.593
I mean, why else
would you be here?

00:22:53.635 --> 00:22:56.001
I can tell you,
I feel much safer now

00:22:56.038 --> 00:22:58.871
just knowing you're along,
because I know...

00:22:58.907 --> 00:23:03.674
I have been holding
this shape for 16 hours.

00:23:03.712 --> 00:23:06.875
I have to revert back
to my liquid state

00:23:06.915 --> 00:23:10.578
but I don't want you to watch
and gawk at me!

00:23:10.619 --> 00:23:14.385
I understand, completely.

00:23:15.924 --> 00:23:19.416
This is a very private moment
and I won't interfere.

00:23:24.233 --> 00:23:25.894
This won't be so bad...

00:23:28.504 --> 00:23:31.701
I have no interest
in speaking to you

00:23:31.740 --> 00:23:35.198
or in listening
to your witless prattle!

00:23:35.244 --> 00:23:37.109
So stay out of my way

00:23:37.146 --> 00:23:40.775
or you'll regret
the day you ever met me!

00:23:55.798 --> 00:23:57.629
Commander, long-range sensors

00:23:57.666 --> 00:24:01.158
have picked up two Jem'Hadar
warships directly ahead.

00:24:01.203 --> 00:24:03.694
They're heading
this way at warp 5.

00:24:03.739 --> 00:24:05.866
How close will they pass us?

00:24:05.908 --> 00:24:07.375
100,000 kilometers.

00:24:07.409 --> 00:24:10.242
That's well within range
of their weapons, Commander.

00:24:10.279 --> 00:24:12.042
Should I alter course?

00:24:12.081 --> 00:24:14.948
No, we need to know if they can
see through the cloaking device

00:24:15.017 --> 00:24:16.541
and this is
as good a time as any.

00:24:16.585 --> 00:24:18.712
Maintain course and speed.

00:24:18.754 --> 00:24:19.721
Red Alert.

00:24:19.755 --> 00:24:21.655
Aye, sir.

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:23.817
Here they come.

00:24:23.859 --> 00:24:26.054
They'll pass us in five seconds.

00:24:26.095 --> 00:24:27.357
On screen.

00:24:27.396 --> 00:24:29.387
Track them.

00:24:29.431 --> 00:24:32.525
They're continuing
on their original heading.

00:24:32.568 --> 00:24:34.365
No indication that they saw us.

00:24:35.404 --> 00:24:36.393
Wait a minute.

00:24:36.438 --> 00:24:38.133
They're changing course.

00:24:38.173 --> 00:24:39.401
Heading this way.

00:24:39.441 --> 00:24:40.965
They must have seen us.

00:24:41.043 --> 00:24:42.704
They're powering
their weapon systems.

00:24:42.744 --> 00:24:45.212
Prepare to de-cloak,
lock phasers on the lead ship...

00:24:45.247 --> 00:24:46.839
No! We may not have
been detected.

00:24:46.882 --> 00:24:47.906
Explain.

00:24:47.950 --> 00:24:50.783
A cloaked ship radiates
a slight subspace variance

00:24:50.819 --> 00:24:51.843
at warp speeds.

00:24:51.887 --> 00:24:53.286
I never heard that.

00:24:53.322 --> 00:24:55.813
It's not something
we've been eager to reveal.

00:24:55.858 --> 00:24:57.792
I suggest dropping out of warp.

00:24:57.826 --> 00:24:59.919
That will eliminate
the variance.

00:24:59.962 --> 00:25:03.398
When they reach our position,
they'll find nothing.

00:25:05.234 --> 00:25:06.326
Do it.

00:25:06.368 --> 00:25:07.494
All stop.

00:25:15.711 --> 00:25:17.440
Commander,
they're sweeping the area

00:25:17.479 --> 00:25:19.276
with some kind
of an anti-proton scan

00:25:19.314 --> 00:25:21.714
and they're being
very thorough about it.

00:25:21.750 --> 00:25:24.082
Will an anti-proton scan
penetrate the cloak?

00:25:24.119 --> 00:25:25.746
That's a good question.

00:25:27.422 --> 00:25:29.117
I'm not sure.

00:25:30.392 --> 00:25:31.450
They're getting closer.

00:25:31.493 --> 00:25:33.222
Commander.

00:25:33.262 --> 00:25:34.957
The Defiant's power signature

00:25:34.997 --> 00:25:37.261
is unusually high
for a ship this size.

00:25:37.299 --> 00:25:40.063
The cloaking device
may not be masking everything.

00:25:43.105 --> 00:25:44.766
Cut main power.

00:25:55.517 --> 00:25:56.984
The other one
has broken off its search.

00:25:57.019 --> 00:25:57.986
It's headed this way.

00:25:58.020 --> 00:26:00.545
Stand by weapons and shields.

00:26:18.807 --> 00:26:21.071
They've gone into warp...

00:26:21.109 --> 00:26:22.838
and resumed
their original course.

00:26:24.313 --> 00:26:25.871
The first thing to go right

00:26:25.914 --> 00:26:28.075
in the Gamma Quadrant
in a long time.

00:26:28.116 --> 00:26:30.607
Let's hope it's not the last.

00:26:40.996 --> 00:26:44.932
Ship's Log, Stardate 48212.4.

00:26:44.967 --> 00:26:46.958
We have arrived
at the Karemma home world

00:26:47.035 --> 00:26:49.765
and opened talks with one
of Quark's business partners

00:26:49.805 --> 00:26:52.501
in an effort to contact
the Founders of the Dominion.

00:26:52.541 --> 00:26:54.338
The Grand Nagus himself

00:26:54.376 --> 00:26:57.834
has sent me as an emissary
on his behalf.

00:26:57.879 --> 00:26:59.540
If you aid us in our mission

00:26:59.581 --> 00:27:02.015
I'm authorized
to increase our purchase

00:27:02.050 --> 00:27:05.850
of tulaberry wine
to the Karemma by three percent.

00:27:05.887 --> 00:27:09.618
Hmm, looks like
a polyduranium alloy blend.

00:27:09.658 --> 00:27:13.526
Interesting, but the metal
has no real value.

00:27:13.562 --> 00:27:16.030
A three percent
increase is negligible.

00:27:16.064 --> 00:27:20.262
I have considerable leeway
to bargain in this circumstance.

00:27:20.302 --> 00:27:21.360
Name your terms.

00:27:21.403 --> 00:27:23.598
Nothing, nothing, nothing.

00:27:23.639 --> 00:27:26.301
The terms are not the issue.

00:27:26.341 --> 00:27:27.706
I cannot help you
locate the Founders

00:27:27.743 --> 00:27:29.301
because I do not know
who they are

00:27:29.344 --> 00:27:31.744
or if they even exist.

00:27:31.780 --> 00:27:32.747
Nothing.

00:27:32.781 --> 00:27:35.716
Ah, here's something
interesting.

00:27:35.751 --> 00:27:37.452
Appears to be
diamide-laced beritium.

00:27:37.452 --> 00:27:39.044
Appears to be
diamide-laced beritium.

00:27:39.086 --> 00:27:41.054
I'll give you 52 diraks for it.

00:27:41.088 --> 00:27:42.055
Done.

00:27:42.089 --> 00:27:43.056
Quark.

00:27:43.090 --> 00:27:44.785
I mean, one bargain
at a time, Ornithar.

00:27:44.826 --> 00:27:46.885
We were talking
about the Founders.

00:27:46.928 --> 00:27:48.725
There is nothing further to say.

00:27:48.763 --> 00:27:49.957
If the Founders exist

00:27:49.997 --> 00:27:52.261
they clearly do not wish
to be contacted

00:27:52.300 --> 00:27:54.097
and that is good enough for me.

00:27:54.135 --> 00:27:56.763
Who's your contact
in the Dominion

00:27:56.804 --> 00:27:59.967
regarding administration,
trade, defense?

00:28:00.041 --> 00:28:01.599
Our only contact
with the Dominion

00:28:01.642 --> 00:28:02.904
has been through the Vorta.

00:28:02.977 --> 00:28:04.911
I have no idea
who they report to.

00:28:05.012 --> 00:28:08.573
All I know is that the Vorta say
to do something and you do it.

00:28:08.616 --> 00:28:10.015
Why?

00:28:10.051 --> 00:28:14.010
Because if you do not, they
will send in the Jem'Hadar...

00:28:14.055 --> 00:28:15.317
and then you die.

00:28:15.356 --> 00:28:17.290
Will you put us in contact
with the Vorta?

00:28:17.325 --> 00:28:19.691
Commander, we do only
as we are told, nothing more.

00:28:19.727 --> 00:28:23.561
And so far, we have not been
told to help you in any way.

00:28:23.598 --> 00:28:25.862
You haven't been told not to,
either.

00:28:25.900 --> 00:28:28.869
No, but I prefer to err
on the side of caution.

00:28:28.903 --> 00:28:30.928
In this case, being cautious
will cost you

00:28:31.005 --> 00:28:32.199
a substantial profit.

00:28:32.240 --> 00:28:33.673
The Ferengi will cease

00:28:33.708 --> 00:28:36.199
purchasing tulaberry
wine immediately.

00:28:36.244 --> 00:28:38.041
If you lost such
a valuable contract

00:28:38.079 --> 00:28:40.707
with the Alpha Quadrant,
it might displease the Vorta.

00:28:40.748 --> 00:28:43.740
They may even send the Jem'Hadar
to find out what happened.

00:28:45.486 --> 00:28:48.978
I will need to access one
of our computers on the surface.

00:28:55.863 --> 00:28:57.694
This is the Callinon system.

00:28:57.732 --> 00:28:59.427
The Dominion maintains

00:28:59.467 --> 00:29:02.061
an unmanned subspace relay
on the seventh planet.

00:29:02.103 --> 00:29:03.627
We have been told by the Vorta

00:29:03.671 --> 00:29:05.434
to direct
all communications there.

00:29:05.473 --> 00:29:09.773
Where the messages are sent
after that is not our concern.

00:29:09.810 --> 00:29:12.802
What is that?

00:29:12.847 --> 00:29:15.907
It is the Omarion Nebula.

00:29:15.950 --> 00:29:21.183
The Omarion Nebula...

00:29:23.791 --> 00:29:27.693
If there is nothing else,
I would like to leave now.

00:29:27.728 --> 00:29:28.786
Of course.

00:29:28.829 --> 00:29:31.423
Uh, Commander, I believe

00:29:31.465 --> 00:29:33.092
I fulfilled my role
in this mission

00:29:33.134 --> 00:29:34.192
so if you don't mind...

00:29:34.235 --> 00:29:36.100
You want to stay behind?

00:29:36.137 --> 00:29:38.037
That was our agreement.

00:29:38.072 --> 00:29:39.039
How can you be sure

00:29:39.073 --> 00:29:40.700
he won't turn you
over to the Dominion

00:29:40.741 --> 00:29:41.708
as soon as we leave?

00:29:41.742 --> 00:29:43.300
He may serve the Dominion

00:29:43.344 --> 00:29:46.370
but I'm the one lining
his pockets with latinum.

00:29:46.414 --> 00:29:47.904
I'll book passage

00:29:47.949 --> 00:29:51.680
on the next ship going
through the wormhole

00:29:51.719 --> 00:29:55.052
and, uh, I'll make a profit
in the process.

00:29:55.089 --> 00:29:56.386
All right, Quark.

00:29:56.424 --> 00:29:58.358
Good luck.

00:29:58.392 --> 00:30:00.257
Same to you, Commander.

00:30:03.364 --> 00:30:04.956
Lay in a course
for the Callinon system.

00:30:05.066 --> 00:30:06.260
Aye, sir.

00:30:17.044 --> 00:30:18.602
Come in.

00:30:21.515 --> 00:30:22.777
Did I wake you?

00:30:22.817 --> 00:30:25.752
Not quite.

00:30:25.786 --> 00:30:27.720
What can I do for you, Major?

00:30:27.755 --> 00:30:29.518
It's about Odo.

00:30:30.925 --> 00:30:32.153
You're worried about him.

00:30:32.193 --> 00:30:33.956
Is it that obvious?

00:30:33.995 --> 00:30:36.463
No, I'm worried about him, too.

00:30:36.497 --> 00:30:40.627
But, at the moment, I don't know
what to do about it.

00:30:40.668 --> 00:30:42.966
Can I speak freely?

00:30:44.405 --> 00:30:46.805
What the hell is wrong
with Starfleet?!

00:30:46.841 --> 00:30:48.240
How could they do this to him?

00:30:48.275 --> 00:30:50.106
This has been a long time
coming, Major.

00:30:50.144 --> 00:30:52.476
Starfleet has never been
happy with the Constable.

00:30:52.513 --> 00:30:54.310
They've been pressing me
to replace him

00:30:54.348 --> 00:30:55.440
for the last two years.

00:30:55.483 --> 00:30:57.917
Because he worked
for the Cardassians.

00:30:57.952 --> 00:30:59.112
No, it goes deeper than that.

00:30:59.153 --> 00:31:01.246
Odo is not what you'd call
a team player.

00:31:01.288 --> 00:31:02.585
Why? Because sometimes he

00:31:02.623 --> 00:31:04.614
doesn't go through
the proper channels?

00:31:04.659 --> 00:31:06.058
Well, that's a start.

00:31:06.093 --> 00:31:07.492
You know Odo.

00:31:07.528 --> 00:31:09.120
He enjoys thumbing his nose
at authority.

00:31:09.163 --> 00:31:12.223
He files reports
when he feels like it.

00:31:12.266 --> 00:31:14.632
His respect for the chain
of command is minimal.

00:31:14.669 --> 00:31:15.897
He gets the job done.

00:31:15.936 --> 00:31:18.268
Starfleet likes team players.

00:31:18.305 --> 00:31:21.138
Starfleet likes
the chain of command

00:31:21.175 --> 00:31:22.972
and, frankly, so do I.

00:31:23.010 --> 00:31:25.103
So you agree
with their decision?

00:31:25.146 --> 00:31:26.909
No, but I understand it.

00:31:26.947 --> 00:31:28.915
And when this mission is over,
you're just going to let him go?

00:31:28.949 --> 00:31:31.179
Look, Major, I want him
to stay as much as you do

00:31:31.218 --> 00:31:32.480
but he has to want to stay.

00:31:32.520 --> 00:31:34.215
Bridge to Commander Sisko.

00:31:34.255 --> 00:31:36.746
We've reached
the Callinon system.

00:31:36.791 --> 00:31:38.486
On my way.

00:31:43.931 --> 00:31:45.899
Ship's Log, supplemental.

00:31:45.933 --> 00:31:47.093
The Defiant has cloaked

00:31:47.134 --> 00:31:49.898
and assumed standard orbit
around Callinon Vll.

00:31:49.937 --> 00:31:51.370
I plan to send Dax and O'Brien

00:31:51.405 --> 00:31:53.703
down to survey the relay station
on the surface.

00:31:53.741 --> 00:31:55.709
According to our sensor sweeps

00:31:55.743 --> 00:31:57.608
it looks like Ornithar
was telling the truth

00:31:57.645 --> 00:31:59.545
when he said the relay
station was unmanned.

00:31:59.580 --> 00:32:03.038
It also appears there are very
few security measures in place.

00:32:03.084 --> 00:32:04.176
Nothing fancy.

00:32:04.218 --> 00:32:05.947
Get in, find what we
need and get out.

00:32:05.986 --> 00:32:06.953
Understood.

00:32:06.987 --> 00:32:08.716
On your way.

00:32:08.756 --> 00:32:12.123
The transporter will need
six seconds to beam them down.

00:32:12.159 --> 00:32:15.151
I want to de-cloak
for exactly six seconds.

00:32:15.196 --> 00:32:16.163
Dax to Bridge.

00:32:16.197 --> 00:32:17.664
We're ready, Benjamin.

00:32:17.698 --> 00:32:18.790
All right.

00:32:18.833 --> 00:32:20.801
Disengage cloak.

00:32:20.835 --> 00:32:22.029
Energize.

00:32:24.772 --> 00:32:26.296
They're on the surface.

00:32:26.340 --> 00:32:28.604
Were we scanned
during transport?

00:32:28.642 --> 00:32:29.768
I don't think so.

00:32:29.810 --> 00:32:31.107
Dax to Defiant.

00:32:31.145 --> 00:32:32.271
Go ahead, Dax.

00:32:32.313 --> 00:32:35.749
We're in what seems to be
the central computer room.

00:32:35.783 --> 00:32:38.445
The user interface
is a little unusual

00:32:38.486 --> 00:32:40.511
but I think we can access it.

00:32:40.554 --> 00:32:42.181
Keep us posted.

00:32:44.358 --> 00:32:46.485
I'm into the main directory.

00:32:46.527 --> 00:32:47.994
That was fast.

00:32:48.095 --> 00:32:49.995
Yes, it was.

00:32:50.030 --> 00:32:51.930
A bit too fast, if you ask me.

00:32:51.966 --> 00:32:53.627
Any indication
that we've tripped

00:32:53.667 --> 00:32:55.225
some kind of
security protocol?

00:32:55.269 --> 00:32:58.466
No, I still have
access to everything.

00:32:58.506 --> 00:33:01.031
Then let's get the information
and get out of here.

00:33:01.075 --> 00:33:02.599
That's fine with me.

00:33:09.049 --> 00:33:11.108
I've should have taken
Quark up on his offer

00:33:11.152 --> 00:33:12.176
for a new replicator.

00:33:12.219 --> 00:33:13.186
Sir?

00:33:13.220 --> 00:33:14.278
Nothing.

00:33:14.321 --> 00:33:16.118
Let's make good use
of this time, Major.

00:33:16.157 --> 00:33:17.818
Begin running a level-3
diagnostic...

00:33:17.858 --> 00:33:18.825
Dax to Defiant.

00:33:18.859 --> 00:33:20.724
I think we have something,
Benjamin.

00:33:20.761 --> 00:33:22.922
We've accessed
a communications log

00:33:22.963 --> 00:33:24.555
of outgoing transmissions.

00:33:24.598 --> 00:33:25.963
From the way I read this, sir

00:33:26.066 --> 00:33:28.193
it looks like 80% %%
of all outgoing traffic

00:33:28.235 --> 00:33:29.702
is sent to one location.

00:33:29.737 --> 00:33:33.764
It's my guess it's either
another relay station

00:33:33.808 --> 00:33:34.832
or a command center.

00:33:34.875 --> 00:33:36.536
Do you have the coordinates?

00:33:36.577 --> 00:33:38.670
I'm sending them to you now.

00:33:41.415 --> 00:33:43.212
We've lost contact with them.

00:33:43.250 --> 00:33:44.615
Get them out of there!

00:33:44.652 --> 00:33:45.710
I can't.

00:33:45.753 --> 00:33:47.653
Some kind of shield has
appeared around the outpost.

00:33:47.688 --> 00:33:48.655
I can't get through it.

00:33:52.626 --> 00:33:54.491
We're picking up three
Jem'Hadar ships, Commander

00:33:54.528 --> 00:33:55.517
heading this way.

00:33:55.563 --> 00:33:57.190
Can we punch
through the security shield

00:33:57.231 --> 00:33:58.994
with our phasers
before the ships get here?

00:33:59.033 --> 00:34:00.000
I'm not sure.

00:34:00.034 --> 00:34:01.467
I've never seen
this kind of field before.

00:34:01.502 --> 00:34:03.868
In order to use the phasers,
we will have to de-cloak.

00:34:03.904 --> 00:34:05.929
That means, we'll be seen
by the Jem'Hadar.

00:34:06.006 --> 00:34:07.371
Well, we've got to do something.

00:34:07.408 --> 00:34:08.739
We can't just leave them there.

00:34:08.776 --> 00:34:10.641
That's exactly
what we should do, Doctor.

00:34:10.678 --> 00:34:11.645
Leave them.

00:34:11.679 --> 00:34:13.647
We came here to locate
the Founders.

00:34:13.681 --> 00:34:15.945
Not to fight the Jem'Hadar

00:34:16.050 --> 00:34:17.779
over two expendable
crew members.

00:34:17.818 --> 00:34:18.944
No one is expendable.

00:34:18.986 --> 00:34:20.453
The Jem'Hadar have
entered the system.

00:34:20.487 --> 00:34:22.387
They'll be in orbit
in 30 seconds.

00:34:32.333 --> 00:34:33.866
Prepare to leave orbit, Major.

00:34:33.999 --> 00:34:34.966
Commander...

00:34:35.000 --> 00:34:36.365
As you were, Doctor.

00:34:36.401 --> 00:34:40.098
Lay in a course
to the coordinates Dax sent us.

00:34:42.808 --> 00:34:44.571
Course laid in.

00:34:44.610 --> 00:34:47.602
Warp 7. Engage.

00:35:03.095 --> 00:35:07.054
What do you think will happen
to Dax and O'Brien?

00:35:07.099 --> 00:35:10.068
They'll probably be held
for interrogation.

00:35:10.102 --> 00:35:12.900
If I know Dax,
she'll use the opportunity

00:35:12.938 --> 00:35:16.032
to try to contact the Founders,
and I intend to do the same.

00:35:16.074 --> 00:35:19.475
Sisko to Odo.
Report to the Bridge, Constable.

00:35:19.511 --> 00:35:21.945
I want to discuss the security
arrangements for our...

00:35:21.980 --> 00:35:24.448
I'm presently indisposed,
Commander.

00:35:24.483 --> 00:35:26.542
Please find someone else
for the job.

00:35:26.585 --> 00:35:28.212
That doesn't sound like Odo.

00:35:28.253 --> 00:35:29.413
No, it doesn't.

00:35:29.454 --> 00:35:31.752
I'd better have a talk with him.

00:35:31.790 --> 00:35:33.087
Uh, let me, sir.

00:35:33.125 --> 00:35:35.593
I think he'll listen to me.

00:35:35.627 --> 00:35:39.085
Three Jem'Hadar ships
have just entered sensor range.

00:35:39.131 --> 00:35:41.656
Bearing 037 mark 215.

00:35:41.700 --> 00:35:43.429
Is there any sign
they've detected us?

00:35:43.468 --> 00:35:44.492
Negative.

00:35:44.536 --> 00:35:46.697
Bring us out of warp
and then cut main power.

00:35:46.738 --> 00:35:48.501
We'll wait here until they pass.

00:35:58.517 --> 00:36:01.145
Odo, it's time we had a talk.

00:36:01.186 --> 00:36:05.680
I'm not going to the Bridge,
so you can save your breath.

00:36:05.724 --> 00:36:09.421
And I'd appreciate being
left alone right now.

00:36:09.461 --> 00:36:13.056
Well, you tried being alone
and it hasn't done any good.

00:36:13.098 --> 00:36:17.000
So maybe it's time to stop
brooding and start talking.

00:36:18.437 --> 00:36:20.564
Are you the ship's counselor
now?

00:36:20.605 --> 00:36:24.405
No... I'm your friend.

00:36:24.443 --> 00:36:26.377
You know, the one
who comes to you

00:36:26.411 --> 00:36:27.639
when she needs help.

00:36:30.215 --> 00:36:33.309
I'm just trying
to return the favor.

00:36:34.353 --> 00:36:36.253
Well, you can return the favor

00:36:36.288 --> 00:36:39.189
by giving me a shuttlecraft
and letting me go.

00:36:39.224 --> 00:36:41.215
Go? Go where?

00:36:41.259 --> 00:36:43.625
We're in the heart
of the Dominion.

00:36:43.662 --> 00:36:46.563
Where the hell do you think
you're gonna go?

00:36:47.632 --> 00:36:49.827
The Omarion Nebula.

00:36:52.504 --> 00:36:53.971
Why?

00:36:54.039 --> 00:36:56.667
I'm not sure why.

00:36:56.708 --> 00:36:59.905
I just know I have to,
that's all.

00:36:59.945 --> 00:37:04.575
Y-You... you're going to have
to do a lot better than that.

00:37:06.952 --> 00:37:09.648
Odo...

00:37:09.688 --> 00:37:10.882
talk to me.

00:37:10.922 --> 00:37:13.584
Tell me what's going on.

00:37:18.430 --> 00:37:21.593
Ever since we've come
into the Gamma Quadrant...

00:37:21.633 --> 00:37:26.536
I've had this feeling...
of being drawn somewhere

00:37:26.571 --> 00:37:32.976
pulled by some instinct
to a specific place...

00:37:34.646 --> 00:37:36.978
the Omarion Nebula.

00:37:38.116 --> 00:37:39.344
Why there?

00:37:40.452 --> 00:37:42.181
I don't know.

00:37:44.623 --> 00:37:45.954
All right.

00:37:47.459 --> 00:37:48.949
Once we've contacted
the Founders

00:37:49.027 --> 00:37:50.289
I'm sure Commander Sisko...

00:37:50.328 --> 00:37:51.852
No!

00:37:51.897 --> 00:37:55.128
Not after we've contacted
the Founders... now!

00:37:55.167 --> 00:37:56.691
I have to leave now!

00:37:56.735 --> 00:37:59.499
Look, I understand
this is important to you

00:37:59.538 --> 00:38:01.165
but we have a mission to...

00:38:04.676 --> 00:38:06.701
Direct hit on the port nacelle!

00:38:06.745 --> 00:38:09.145
How did they see through
the cloaking device?

00:38:09.181 --> 00:38:10.910
They might have analyzed
the sensor information

00:38:10.982 --> 00:38:12.472
on the anti-proton scan

00:38:12.517 --> 00:38:14.280
and found a way
to penetrate the cloak.

00:38:15.487 --> 00:38:17.546
We'll have to save
the speculation for later.

00:38:17.589 --> 00:38:21.355
Disengage the cloak, raise the
shields and fire on my command!

00:38:36.274 --> 00:38:38.936
Communications
and long-range sensors are out!

00:38:38.977 --> 00:38:40.740
What's the status
of the warp drive?

00:38:40.779 --> 00:38:42.576
The starboard power coupling
is destroyed!

00:38:42.614 --> 00:38:45.048
I'm trying
to reroute main power!

00:38:51.523 --> 00:38:52.820
He's gone!

00:38:52.858 --> 00:38:53.984
I'll take the helm!

00:38:55.660 --> 00:38:57.321
Locking onto the lead ship!

00:38:57.362 --> 00:38:58.659
- Ready?
- Ready!

00:38:58.697 --> 00:38:59.686
Fire!

00:39:05.003 --> 00:39:08.370
The other two are moving
out of phaser range.

00:39:08.406 --> 00:39:11.204
They're coming back
for another pass.

00:39:11.243 --> 00:39:13.837
They're moving
a little slower now.

00:39:13.879 --> 00:39:15.904
They'll be
more cautious this time.

00:39:16.014 --> 00:39:18.278
Doctor, use
evasive pattern delta-5.

00:39:18.316 --> 00:39:21.683
We need to keep them off balance
until we get warp power back.

00:39:21.720 --> 00:39:22.812
Aye, sir.

00:39:27.325 --> 00:39:29.156
Are you all right?

00:39:29.194 --> 00:39:30.388
Just a few bruises.

00:39:30.428 --> 00:39:32.123
Kira to Bridge.

00:39:32.164 --> 00:39:34.098
Kira to Bridge!

00:39:34.132 --> 00:39:36.726
We have to get up there.

00:39:38.170 --> 00:39:40.400
T'Rul, where's my warp power?

00:39:40.438 --> 00:39:43.100
I can't get the phase inducers
to align

00:39:43.141 --> 00:39:44.108
with the ODN matrixes!

00:39:44.142 --> 00:39:46.133
Commander, three more
Jem'Hadar warships

00:39:46.178 --> 00:39:47.668
approaching off the port bow!

00:39:47.712 --> 00:39:50.078
Full impulse!
Get us out of here!

00:39:51.616 --> 00:39:53.208
We've lost main power.

00:39:53.251 --> 00:39:55.378
We've got to get to a shuttle.

00:39:55.420 --> 00:39:57.945
Our duty is to get to the Bridge
and help defend the ship.

00:39:58.056 --> 00:40:01.219
If main power is out,
then the shields are out, Kira.

00:40:01.259 --> 00:40:02.726
The ship is defenseless!

00:40:14.739 --> 00:40:16.639
Main power is off-line!

00:40:16.675 --> 00:40:18.939
The shields have collapsed!

00:40:18.977 --> 00:40:20.911
I've lost helm control.

00:40:20.946 --> 00:40:23.244
Inertial dampers failing.

00:40:23.281 --> 00:40:24.578
Ready escape pods.

00:40:24.616 --> 00:40:26.584
Prepare to abandon ship.

00:41:25.777 --> 00:41:27.438
Where am I?

00:41:29.114 --> 00:41:31.582
You're in a shuttlecraft.

00:41:31.616 --> 00:41:33.049
You were wounded.

00:41:33.084 --> 00:41:34.284
Try not to move around.

00:41:42.125 --> 00:41:44.252
Odo, what happened?

00:41:44.294 --> 00:41:46.319
We were under attack.

00:41:48.064 --> 00:41:49.793
The ship was boarded.

00:41:49.832 --> 00:41:52.357
You were wounded in the attack.

00:41:52.402 --> 00:41:55.235
I managed to get us
to the shuttlecraft

00:41:55.271 --> 00:41:58.001
but I don't know
much more than that.

00:41:58.041 --> 00:42:02.944
The last time I saw the Defiant,
she was dead in space

00:42:02.979 --> 00:42:06.380
and surrounded
by Jem'Hadar ships.

00:42:06.416 --> 00:42:08.281
Sisko? Bashir?

00:42:10.420 --> 00:42:11.910
I don't know.

00:42:23.032 --> 00:42:24.465
Where are we?

00:42:24.500 --> 00:42:29.096
We're approaching
the Omarion Nebula.

00:42:29.138 --> 00:42:31.299
You should have taken us
back to the wormhole.

00:42:32.442 --> 00:42:34.376
You didn't object at the time.

00:42:34.410 --> 00:42:36.275
I was unconscious.

00:42:42.118 --> 00:42:43.449
You found anything?

00:42:49.726 --> 00:42:52.524
That's a Class-M planet.

00:42:52.562 --> 00:42:53.824
No star system.

00:42:53.863 --> 00:42:55.490
A rogue planet?

00:42:55.531 --> 00:42:57.556
Yes.

00:44:20.750 --> 00:44:22.513
Welcome home.
